-- title:
--   Surjectivity of Gauss reduction onto κ(X₁(M))
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and a nonzero level $M$ with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$, a field $L$ of characteristic zero that is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of order $p$, and a primitive $p$-th root of unity $\zeta \in L$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L((q)) =$ `LaurentSeries L` over $L$ which equals `laurentBaseChange L (x1FunctionField M)`, i.e. the $L$-subfield of $L((q))$ generated by the image of `x1FunctionFieldC ℚ M` under the coefficientwise map `coeffEmb L` induced by $\mathbb{Q} \to L$, where `x1FunctionFieldC ℚ M` is the intermediate field of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ generated by `intFormRatiosC ℚ (Gamma1 M)`. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with an algebra structure over $L$ making $L$ its fraction field, with $p$ in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ in the image of $A$, equipped with an algebra structure on $K$ compatible with that on $L$; write $\kappa$ for the residue field of $A$. Let $j \in K$ have image `coeffEmb L jq` in $L((q))$, with $j \ne 0$. Then for every $z \in \kappa((q))$ lying in `x1FunctionFieldC κ M`, the $\kappa$-subfield generated by `intFormRatiosC κ (Gamma1 M)`, there are $f \in K$ and power series $x, y \in A[[q]]$ such that the reduction of $y$ modulo the maximal ideal is nonzero, $f \cdot y = x$ holds in $L((q))$ after pushing the coefficients of $x$ and $y$ to $L$, and the quotient of the reductions, $\bar{x}/\bar{y}$, equals $z$ in $\kappa((q))$.
--
--   This is the surjectivity statement for reduction of Gauss-presented functions: every element of the $q$-expansion function field of $X_1(M)$ over the residue field $\kappa$ arises as $\bar{x}/\bar{y}$ for a presentation $f \cdot y = x$ of some $f$ in the base-changed function field $K$. It is used in [`ModularCurve.XOne.chartRing_le_adjoin_gaussReductions_chartAlg_x1`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XOne.chartRing_le_adjoin_gaussReductions_chartAlg_x1) to show that the chart ring over $\kappa$ is contained in the algebra generated by such Gauss reductions.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_XOneP_exists_gaussPresentation_reduction_eq_of_mem_x1FunctionFieldC_of_x1.lean

